menu "JARVIS satellite"

config JARVIS_ENABLE_ESP_SR
    bool "Audio front-end: AEC + VAD (hands-free voice barge-in)"
    default n
    help
        Route the microphone through the Espressif ESP-SR audio front-end
        (AFE) on the ESP32-P4.

        Without this the panel is push-to-talk: the mic is opened only on a tap
        and is closed while the reply plays, so it cannot hear you mid-answer
        and every turn starts with a tap.

        With this enabled the AFE adds

          * AEC - subtracts the panel's own playback from the mic signal, so
                  the mic can stay open while J.A.R.V.I.S. talks (voice
                  barge-in: just start speaking to interrupt);
          * NS  - neural noise suppression ahead of ASR;
          * VAD - a real voice-activity detector for end-of-speech, which is
                  steadier than the raw RMS gate and cuts the trailing pause.

        Enabling this compiles in the espressif/esp-sr (and esp-dl) components,
        adds a `model` flash partition for the AFE models and requires the
        model image to be flashed next to the app. The dedicated
        `jarvis-panel-sr` PlatformIO environment wires all of that up; build it
        instead of `jarvis-panel`.

        Leave this off (the default) for the original push-to-talk firmware.
        When off, esp-sr is not even downloaded (the dependency in
        src/idf_component.yml is gated on this symbol), so the default build is
        byte-for-byte unchanged.

endmenu
